  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;STEPHEN RALPH CARTWRIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stephen Ralph Cartwright is a scion of the esteemed Cartwright family, known for his distinguished military service and later for his marriage to Lady Fanny Hay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen Ralph Cartwright is an ancestor whose personal life has recently been discovered, bringing interest from his descendants."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LADY FANNY HAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Fanny Hay is a member of the aristocratic Hay family, known for her beauty, intelligence, and her marriage to Stephen Ralph Cartwright."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE FORGOTTEN UNION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Forgotten Union is the title of a document or book that explores the hidden marriage of Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Lady Fanny Hay."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CARTWRIGHT FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cartwright Family is a distinguished family known for their military service and conservative values."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE HAY FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Hay Family is a prominent aristocratic family known for their connections to the royal court and extensive landholdings in Scotland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"London is the setting for the rumors and whispers surrounding the marriage between Stephen and Fanny."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF OXFORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Oxford is the institution where historians have uncovered new evidence about the marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Elizabeth Helen Rutt."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELIZABETH HELEN RUTT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elizabeth Helen Rutt is a member of the esteemed peerage, known for her marriage to Stephen Ralph Cartwright and her family's wealth and influence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUTT MANOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rutt Manor is the family estate of Elizabeth Helen Rutt, one of the largest and most prestigious in the country."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LADY CHARLOTTE CARTWRIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Charlotte Cartwright is the sister of Stephen Ralph Cartwright and a witness to the marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LADY VICTORIA RUTT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Victoria Rutt is a descendant of Elizabeth Helen Rutt and provides insight into her family's history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAMES CARTWRIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"James Cartwright is a great-great-grandson of Stephen Ralph Cartwright and interested in learning more about his ancestor's personal life."&lt;SEP&gt;"James Cartwright is a great-great-grandson of Stephen Ralph Cartwright, expressing gratitude and interest in the new information about their family's history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;19TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 19th century is the historical period during which the marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Lady Fanny Hay took place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ARISTOCRACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British aristocracy is the social class within which the marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Lady Fanny Hay occurred."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLANDESTINE MARRIAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A clandestine marriage is the secret marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Lady Fanny Hay, which remained hidden from society."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rumors of a clandestine marriage between Stephen and Fanny began to circulate among the aristocratic circles of London."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIVATE CEREMONY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A private ceremony is the type of marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Elizabeth Helen Rutt, which was kept out of the public eye."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSERVATIVE VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conservative values refer to the Cartwright family's traditional and cautious approach to marriage and social norms."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL NORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Social norms refer to the expectations and behaviors expected within the Hay and Cartwright families."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTIMATE AFFAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An intimate affair is how Cartwright's sister, Lady Charlotte Cartwright, described the wedding between Stephen and Elizabeth Helen Rutt."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEALTH AND INFLUENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wealth and influence refer to the significant financial and social standing brought to the marriage by Elizabeth Helen Rutt."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVOTED COUPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A devoted couple refers to the relationship between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Elizabeth Helen Rutt, described as bringing great joy to both families."&lt;SEP&gt;"The devoted couple is mentioned as a unit, bringing joy to both families."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIRELESS EFFORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tireless efforts are attributed to the researchers who have provided new information about the family's history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tireless efforts refer to the dedication of the researchers at the University of Oxford in uncovering the evidence of the marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARTWRIGHT'S DESCENDANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cartwright's descendants are a group of people interested in learning more about their ancestor's personal life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOTH FAMILIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Both families are the beneficiaries of the devoted couple's union, experiencing great joy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISCOVERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The discovery of personal information about Stephen Ralph Cartwright has sparked interest among his descendants."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREAT JOY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Great joy is experienced by both families due to the devoted couple's union."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0378</data>
    </node>
